Comparison: Java vs. Go for Migration UtilitiesFeatureJava (Current Expertise)Go (Golang)Development SpeedHigh (No learning curve for your team).Medium (Simple syntax, but team must learn "the Go way").Tooling/LibrariesVast (Excellent for parsing XML/JSON, SOAP, and Akana specificities).Good (Great for REST/JSON, but may lack niche legacy libraries).DeploymentRequires JRE/JDK installation on the target machine.Single Binary (Self-contained, no runtime needed).Memory/StartupHigher overhead; "Warm-up" time for the JVM.Minimal; Instant startup and very low RAM usage.ConcurrencyMature (Virtual Threads/ExecutorService).Built-in (Goroutines are extremely lightweight).Error HandlingExceptions (try-catch).Explicit (if err != nil).MaintainabilityHigh (Team already knows the patterns).High (Language is designed for readability).
